      "text_raw": "A similar voltage clamp is\nused in the circuit in this\nslide. Transistors Q3 and Q4\nmaintain a 0.7 V voltage\ndrop across the input tran-\nsistors Q1,2. These devices\nare normally super-beta\ntransistors. Their v ’s must\nCE\ntherefore be small indeed.\nTheir base currents are\ndrawn from a current\nmirror, which derives its\ninput current from the base\nof transistor Q5. This tran-\nsistor must therefore be well\nmatched to the input\ndevices. Indeed, it is the same as for the input devices. Its current is also the same.\nThe actual currents are shown on the next slide.",
      "text": "A similar voltage clamp is used in the circuit in this slide. Transistors Q3 and Q4 maintain a 0.7 V voltage drop across the input transistors Q1,2. These devices are normally super-beta transistors. Their v ’s must CE therefore be small indeed. Their base currents are drawn from a current mirror, which derives its input current from the base of transistor Q5. This transistor must therefore be well matched to the input devices. Indeed, it is the same as for the input devices. Its current is also the same. The actual currents are shown on the next slide."
